=============================================================
  Cointegration Diagnostics
=============================================================

=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=1)   logL =     -20.0579540523
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=1)   logL =     -14.5698646497
                                 sum  =     -34.6278187020
                                 joint=     -34.6278187020
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is -34.6278400446)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -7.567e-12   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED

  --- optimality certificate ---
  logL AT the values brought in   =     -42.7340486882
  logL of the diagonal fit        =     -34.6278400446
  optimality gap (fit - brought)  = +8.106e+00

  The gap is >= 0 always, and zero exactly when what came in were
  the univariate optima.  Here they were not: this input is A SPECIFICATION.


